# Virtualenv. NEVER committed. task.txt section 1: the rename broke every
# console script in .venv/bin because the shebang pointed at a path that no
# longer existed. A committed venv ships that class of bug to everyone.
.venv/
venv/

# Byte-compiled / build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches. All three are regenerated by the first command that needs
# them, and none of them is a measurement anyone should read from history.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage data. The .coverage file is a MEASUREMENT, and a committed one goes
# stale silently: it looks current and it is not. AGENTS.md records a session
# that quoted stale coverage as fresh.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Built bundles. `xat-practice build` regenerates out/ from source in one
# command, so committing it would put a second copy of every lesson in the
# history where it can drift from the code that produced it.
out/

# Local secrets. python-dotenv is a dependency for the future LLM client; this
# is where a real key would go, and it must never be staged.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store